1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:19,428
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya, your host. Today is May twenty-fourth. This is our very first episode. Today's story: more foreigners are visiting Japan than ever before. The number just passed thirty million. Let's listen.

2
00:00:20,027 --> 00:00:27,564
[News] 去年、日本に来た外国人の数が3000万人を超えました。

3
00:00:28,263 --> 00:00:37,384
[News] 一番多い国は中国です。次は韓国、そしてアメリカです。

4
00:00:38,084 --> 00:00:45,835
[News] 外国人に人気がある場所は、東京、大阪、京都です。

5
00:00:46,536 --> 00:00:53,496
[News] 最近は、北海道や沖縄に行く人も増えています。

6
00:00:54,195 --> 00:01:01,396
[News] 外国人がたくさん来るので、ホテルの値段が高くなっています。

7
00:01:02,095 --> 00:01:14,215
[News] 日本語が分からなくて困る外国人もいます。駅やレストランで、英語のメニューや案内が増えています。

8
00:01:14,915 --> 00:01:22,763
[News] 日本政府は、「もっと多くの外国人に来てほしい」と言っています。

9
00:01:23,463 --> 00:01:31,144
[Host] All right. This story uses simple, everyday Japanese. Perfect for beginners. Let's break it down.

10
00:01:31,743 --> 00:01:33,519
[Host] The first sentence.

11
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:42,183
[Slow] 去年、日本に来た外国人の数が3000万人を超えました。

12
00:01:42,983 --> 00:01:50,280
[Host] Last year, the number of foreigners who came to Japan exceeded thirty million. Let's look at the key words.

13
00:01:50,879 --> 00:01:52,896
[Vocab] 去年

14
00:01:53,296 --> 00:01:56,968
[Host] Last year. One of the first time words you learn.

15
00:01:57,567 --> 00:02:00,183
[Vocab] 外国人

16
00:02:00,584 --> 00:02:07,376
[Host] Foreigner. The three characters mean outside, country, person. Very logical.

17
00:02:07,975 --> 00:02:10,448
[Vocab] 超えました

18
00:02:10,848 --> 00:02:16,151
[Host] Exceeded, passed. When a number goes over a target, you use this verb.

19
00:02:16,752 --> 00:02:18,527
[Host] Where are the visitors from?

20
00:02:19,127 --> 00:02:28,895
[Slow] 一番多い国は中国です。次は韓国、そしてアメリカです。

21
00:02:29,695 --> 00:02:35,312
[Host] The country with the most visitors is China. Next is South Korea, then America.

22
00:02:35,912 --> 00:02:38,816
[Vocab] 一番多い

23
00:02:39,216 --> 00:02:47,111
[Host] The most. The first word means number one, the second means many. Together: the most numerous.

24
00:02:47,711 --> 00:02:49,463
[Vocab] 次

25
00:02:49,864 --> 00:02:54,183
[Host] Next. Short and useful. You'll hear it everywhere.

26
00:02:54,783 --> 00:02:56,632
[Host] What places are popular?

27
00:02:57,231 --> 00:03:05,560
[Slow] 外国人に人気がある場所は、東京、大阪、京都です。

28
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:11,376
[Host] The places popular with foreigners are Tokyo, Osaka, and Kyoto.

29
00:03:11,975 --> 00:03:14,639
[Vocab] 人気がある

30
00:03:15,039 --> 00:03:23,776
[Host] Popular. Literally, it means has people's spirit. You can use this for anything — a restaurant, a song, a person.

31
00:03:24,376 --> 00:03:26,463
[Vocab] 場所

32
00:03:26,864 --> 00:03:31,207
[Host] Place, location. A basic but very important word.

33
00:03:31,807 --> 00:03:33,391
[Host] And new trends.

34
00:03:33,991 --> 00:03:41,455
[Slow] 最近は、北海道や沖縄に行く人も増えています。

35
00:03:42,256 --> 00:03:48,063
[Host] Recently, the number of people going to Hokkaido and Okinawa is also increasing.

36
00:03:48,663 --> 00:03:51,015
[Vocab] 最近

37
00:03:51,415 --> 00:03:56,599
[Host] Recently. Use it at the beginning of a sentence to talk about current trends.

38
00:03:57,199 --> 00:03:59,864
[Vocab] 増えています

39
00:04:00,264 --> 00:04:07,032
[Host] Is increasing. The ongoing form means it's a change that's still happening. Very common in news.

40
00:04:07,632 --> 00:04:09,240
[Host] There's a side effect.

41
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:17,567
[Slow] 外国人がたくさん来るので、ホテルの値段が高くなっています。

42
00:04:18,367 --> 00:04:22,783
[Host] Because many foreigners are coming, hotel prices have gone up.

43
00:04:23,384 --> 00:04:25,663
[Vocab] たくさん

44
00:04:26,064 --> 00:04:29,975
[Host] A lot, many. Very basic, very useful.

45
00:04:30,576 --> 00:04:32,663
[Vocab] 値段

46
00:04:33,064 --> 00:04:37,384
[Host] Price. You can say the price is high, or the price is cheap.

47
00:04:37,983 --> 00:04:39,591
[Host] And a challenge.

48
00:04:40,192 --> 00:04:46,072
[Slow] 日本語が分からなくて困る外国人もいます。

49
00:04:46,872 --> 00:04:51,096
[Host] There are also foreigners who don't understand Japanese and have trouble.

50
00:04:51,696 --> 00:04:54,216
[Vocab] 分からない

51
00:04:54,615 --> 00:04:58,911
[Host] Don't understand. One of the most important verbs in Japanese.

52
00:04:59,512 --> 00:05:01,600
[Vocab] 困る

53
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:08,672
[Host] To be in trouble, to have difficulty. When you're lost in Japan and can't read the signs — that feeling.

54
00:05:09,271 --> 00:05:10,663
[Host] The solution.

55
00:05:11,264 --> 00:05:18,512
[Slow] 駅やレストランで、英語のメニューや案内が増えています。

56
00:05:19,312 --> 00:05:24,543
[Host] At stations and restaurants, English menus and guides are increasing.

57
00:05:25,144 --> 00:05:27,399
[Vocab] 案内

58
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:32,000
[Host] Guide, information. You'll see this on signs everywhere.

59
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:34,567
[Host] And what the government says.

60
00:05:35,168 --> 00:05:43,351
[Slow] 日本政府は、もっと多くの外国人に来てほしいと言っています。

61
00:05:44,151 --> 00:05:48,279
[Host] The Japanese government says they want even more foreigners to come.

62
00:05:48,879 --> 00:05:51,016
[Vocab] もっと

63
00:05:51,415 --> 00:05:56,456
[Host] More, even more. A very handy word for everyday conversation.

64
00:05:57,055 --> 00:05:59,696
[Vocab] 来てほしい

65
00:06:00,096 --> 00:06:07,824
[Host] Want someone to come. This pattern means you want someone else to do something. It's different from when you say what you yourself want to do.

66
00:06:08,423 --> 00:06:11,423
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

67
00:06:12,024 --> 00:06:19,560
[News] 去年、日本に来た外国人の数が3000万人を超えました。

68
00:06:20,259 --> 00:06:29,379
[News] 一番多い国は中国です。次は韓国、そしてアメリカです。

69
00:06:30,079 --> 00:06:37,831
[News] 外国人に人気がある場所は、東京、大阪、京都です。

70
00:06:38,531 --> 00:06:45,492
[News] 最近は、北海道や沖縄に行く人も増えています。

71
00:06:46,192 --> 00:06:53,391
[News] 外国人がたくさん来るので、ホテルの値段が高くなっています。

72
00:06:54,091 --> 00:07:06,211
[News] 日本語が分からなくて困る外国人もいます。駅やレストランで、英語のメニューや案内が増えています。

73
00:07:06,911 --> 00:07:14,759
[News] 日本政府は、「もっと多くの外国人に来てほしい」と言っています。

74
00:07:15,459 --> 00:07:18,196
[Host] Quiz time. Three questions.

75
00:07:18,795 --> 00:07:24,915
[Slow] 去年、何人の外国人が日本に来ましたか？

76
00:07:25,716 --> 00:07:30,444
[Host] How many foreigners came to Japan last year? Over thirty million.

77
00:07:31,043 --> 00:07:35,315
[Slow] 一番多い国はどこですか？

78
00:07:36,115 --> 00:07:39,572
[Host] Which country has the most visitors? China.

79
00:07:40,172 --> 00:07:44,732
[Slow] ホテルの値段はどうなっていますか？

80
00:07:45,531 --> 00:07:49,012
[Host] What's happening to hotel prices? They're going up.

81
00:07:49,612 --> 00:08:02,788
[Host] That's the first episode of Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

82
00:08:03,387 --> 00:08:05,788
[News] また明日。
